import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="About | Enterprise IT Fixes" description="A practical reference library of enterprise IT troubleshooting guides, built around common issues and linked vendor sources.">
  <div class="page"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'About'}]} /><p class="eyebrow">About this project</p><h1 class="page-title">Practical notes for solving IT problems.</h1><p class="page-lead">Enterprise IT Fixes is an independently maintained reference library for IT administrators. It brings focused troubleshooting paths and primary vendor references together, without claiming affiliation with the vendors mentioned.</p>
    <div class="about-grid section"><section class="about-card"><h2>What each guide should do</h2><p>Each guide starts with a specific error or symptom, then helps separate plausible causes before suggesting a change. The right diagnosis can differ between environments, so use the stated scope and checks rather than treating a common fix as universal.</p></section><section class="about-card"><h2>Sources and limits</h2><p>Technical claims link to vendor or standards documentation so readers can check current behavior. A suggested procedure is not presented as a test result: the guide should say when a version, setting, or outcome was not established. Follow the source documentation and your change process before making production changes.</p></section><section class="about-card"><h2>How guides are prepared</h2><p>Guides may be based on sanitized troubleshooting notes or on research into a specific technical question. Drafting tools, including AI, may assist with organization and wording; they are not evidence. Source links and environment-specific checks are included so readers can verify the advice for their own setup.</p></section></div>
    <section class="info-panel"><h2>Suggest a correction</h2><p>There is no account system, comment box, newsletter, or contact form on this site. If a technical statement needs correction, use the public repository's issue tracker.</p><a class="button" href="https://github.com/mantha0007-cell/enterprise-it-fixes/issues">Open a repository issue</a></section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
